 "alert_rule": {
  "definition": "up_move = close[i] - min(close over the previous window) (the leg is measured OFF THE WINDOW LOW); down_move = max(close over the previous window) - close[i] (measured off the window HIGH). Fire 'up' when up_move >= max(down_move, threshold); otherwise fire 'down' when down_move >= max(up_move, threshold) - the stronger leg of the two wins, so one run in one direction prints one alert. Re-arm once |close[i] - anchor| <= the re-arm band. The window is measured in MINUTES and converted to candles per candle interval, and windows that start at or after index i are skipped. (An earlier copy of this string described a breakout off the prior extreme, which is not what the code does; both runtimes are pinned by the same reference vectors.)",
